WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:03.968
This slide is very important because the two
conditions look similar but

00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:08.824
they do not mean the same thing In the first version
SQL

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.349
evaluates the AND portion before the OR portion This
means the consent

00:00:13.362 --> 00:00:17.343
requirement does not necessarily apply to every
patient selected by the age

00:00:17.356 --> 00:00:22.614
condition In the second version we put age or
diagnosis inside parentheses

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:28.094
and then require consent for the entire group You
have both versions

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:34.197
in the code cell Before you click Run make a
prediction Which

00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:37.728
patient might appear in the first result but
disappear in the second

00:00:39.134 --> 00:00:43.156
Then run the code in the browser and compare the
outputs You

00:00:43.182 --> 00:00:46.571
can also copy both queries into pgAdmin and run them
one at

00:00:46.596 --> 00:00:50.630
a time This is a good example of why parentheses are
part

00:00:50.643 --> 00:00:53.001
of the meaning of the rule not just formatting
